      "body": "Complete (a5a1e63). DoD status: (1) ci.yml gains the gate-c-trend job: runs scripts/gate_c_trend.sh on every push/PR — the real Gate C measurement on the fixture corpus, compared against the pinned record docs/transformerless/gate_c_pinned.json (maintainer-bumped like the kappa baseline). (2) Alarm thresholds per the pin: top-1 drop > 0.02 abs or bits/token regression > 0.1 abs vs pinned, on EITHER the Rule 1+2 or the baseline row (a baseline regression is itself a signal worth stopping for). (3) Alarm path demonstrated end-to-end: exit 1 on a synthetic regression (pinned top-1 = 0.99 vs measured 0.3171) with the regression named in CI-readable output; exit 0 on the clean run. (4) Trend JSONL (commit sha + timestamp + the four metrics) uploads as a 90-day CI artifact per run for curve plotting; threshold and artifact location documented in the pin file and workflow.",
